## The resolution chain

Three tiers, tried in order:

```
Tier 1: OXC static  (handles ~90%)
  → Known type patterns (cva, SxProps, HTMLChakraProps...)
  → Utility types (Omit, Pick, Partial, Exclude, Extract...)
  → Template literal expansion
  → Indexed access table for known React types
  → Everything else: emit RawOpaque and collect for Tier 2

Tier 2: typescript-go  (handles ~8%, opt-in)
  → Conditional types: T extends U ? X : Y
  → Mapped types: { [K in Keys]: Value }
  → Complex indexed access: NonNullable<HTMLAttributes<E>["tabIndex"]>
  → ReturnType<typeof fn>, Parameters<typeof fn>
  → SxProps<Theme>, SystemProps<Theme>
  → Parse display string response → try to build PropType from it
  → If parse fails: emit Opaque with improved raw string from typescript-go

Tier 3: Opaque  (always available, ~2%)
  → Module augmentation results
  → Runtime-dependent types (too complex even for typescript-go)
  → typescript-go unavailable (emit diagnostic explaining how to enable)
```

