**New `OpaqueReason` variants to mark "worth querying typescript-go":**
```rust
pub enum OpaqueReason {
    // ...existing...
    ConditionalType,   // T extends U ? X : Y — typescript-go can resolve
    MappedType,        // { [K in Keys]: V } — typescript-go can resolve
    IndexedAccess,     // Type["key"] — typescript-go can resolve
    // ...existing others stay as-is (module augmentation, runtime-dependent, etc.)
}

impl OpaqueReason {
    /// Whether typescript-go resolution should be attempted for this reason
    pub fn can_resolve_with_type_checker(&self) -> bool {
        matches!(self,
            OpaqueReason::ConditionalType |
            OpaqueReason::MappedType |
            OpaqueReason::IndexedAccess |
            OpaqueReason::DepthExceeded
        )
    }
}
```

The pipeline then collects all `Opaque` props where `can_resolve_with_type_checker()` is true, batches them, and invokes the subprocess at the end of static resolution.

