## Fix 1: DTS cache is dead code — wire it into the pipeline

In `crates/core/src/pipeline.rs`, `extract()` loads and saves the DTS cache but never calls `cache.get()` or `cache.insert()`. Add cache consultation for `.d.ts` files only (`.d.ts` files don't change during a run; source `.ts`/`.tsx` do):

In the parallel parse phase, change the map closure to check the cache first for `.d.ts` files:

```rust
let source_data_vec: Vec<(Utf8PathBuf, SourceData)> = src_files
    .par_iter()
    .map(|path| {
        // For .d.ts files, check the DTS cache first
        let is_dts = path.as_str().ends_with(".d.ts");
        if is_dts {
            if let Some(cached) = cache.get(path) {
                return (path.clone(), cached);
            }
        }
        let source = std::fs::read_to_string(path).unwrap_or_default();
        let data = crate::extractor::parse_file(path, &source);
        // Cache .d.ts results for future runs
        if is_dts {
            cache.insert(path, data.clone());
        }
        (path.clone(), data)
    })
    .collect();
```

Note: `DtsCache` is not `Sync` because `DashMap` is... actually DashMap IS Sync. But `cache` is a local variable not an `Arc`, so rayon's parallel iterator can't share it without `Arc`. Fix: wrap in `Arc`:

```rust
let cache = Arc::new(DtsCache::load_from_disk(options.cache_dir.as_deref()));
let cache_ref = Arc::clone(&cache);
let source_data_vec: Vec<(Utf8PathBuf, SourceData)> = src_files
    .par_iter()
    .map(|path| {
        let is_dts = path.as_str().ends_with(".d.ts");
        if is_dts {
            if let Some(cached) = cache_ref.get(path) {
                return (path.clone(), cached);
            }
        }
        let source = std::fs::read_to_string(path).unwrap_or_default();
        let data = crate::extractor::parse_file(path, &source);
        if is_dts { cache_ref.insert(path, data.clone()); }
        (path.clone(), data)
    })
    .collect();
// ... rest of extract()
Arc::try_unwrap(cache).unwrap_or_else(|a| (*a).clone_shallow_fallback()).save_to_disk();
```

Actually `DtsCache` doesn't have `clone_shallow_fallback`. Simpler: `Arc::try_unwrap(cache)` will succeed because all rayon workers have finished. If it fails, just call save on the Arc:

```rust
let cache = Arc::new(DtsCache::load_from_disk(options.cache_dir.as_deref()));
// ... extraction with cache_ref = Arc::clone(&cache)
// After collect():
match Arc::try_unwrap(cache) {
    Ok(c) => c.save_to_disk(),
    Err(arc) => arc.save_to_disk(),  // DtsCache::save_to_disk takes &self, so this works
}
```

Also update `ExtractionStats.dts_cache_hits` counter — add a `AtomicU32` to count cache hits and set `stats.dts_cache_hits`:

```rust
let cache_hits = std::sync::atomic::AtomicU32::new(0);
// In the closure, after cache hit: cache_hits.fetch_add(1, Ordering::Relaxed);
// After collect: stats.dts_cache_hits = cache_hits.load(Ordering::Relaxed);
```

